    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d995">

                <pb facs="0872" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/241.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-22T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1912—12 noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am informed by the American colony committee that they desire 1,000
                    Krag-Jorgensen rifles at price stated and 250,000 cartridges therefor, to be
                    shipped by Ward Line steamer leaving New York [next Thursday?].</p>
                <p>Attention is called to the fact that the military attaché has no right of entry,
                    and I request instructions as to course resulting therefrom.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
